msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:216
msgid "Strict mode"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:221
msgid "Report readme.txt / readme.md changes as findings instead of suppressing them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:224
msgid "By default, changes limited to readme.txt/readme.md are treated as a low-risk \"soft change\" and suppressed automatically. Enable strict mode to see every difference, including those files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:231
msgid "Stat-based change detection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:236
msgid "Track file size and timestamps of plugins that cannot be verified against checksums, and report changes since the previous run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:239
msgid "Applies to custom or premium plugins and mu-plugin loaders that have no official checksums. The first run only records a baseline. When a plugin version changes, its baseline is rebuilt without reporting changes. File contents are not read unless content-hash comparison is also enabled below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:246
msgid "Content-hash comparison for custom plugins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:251
msgid "Also compute a content hash for custom/premium plugins and mu-plugin loaders, and report a change even when file size and modified time stay the same."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:254
msgid "Detects a same-size rewrite that preserves the timestamp, which size/timestamp tracking alone cannot catch. This reads file contents on every run and adds I/O cost, so it is off by default; consider enabling it only for sites with a small number of custom plugins. Files larger than a fixed size limit fall back to size/timestamp tracking only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:261
msgid "Unrecorded version change alerts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:266
msgid "Alert on version changes that did not go through the WordPress updater."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:269
msgid "Turn this off on sites that deploy via git, FTP, or Composer, where legitimate version changes never produce an update event."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:276
msgid "GitHub repository mappings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-wpcv-page-settings.php:281
msgid "Verify a plugin or theme against the assets of its GitHub Release instead of wordpress.org. One mapping per line: plugin:{slug} or theme:{stylesheet}, then owner/repo, then optionally the start of the asset file name. The Release is found by the installed version (tag \"1.2.3\" or \"v1.2.3\"). Plugins and themes that are not listed are verified as before. Invalid lines and repeated targets are dropped when saving; comment lines (starting with #) are not kept. Directories that contain a .git entry are never compared with GitHub."
msgstr ""

